<%# ONE CALL'S PROMPT AS SENT AND ANSWER AS RECEIVED, collapsed.

    THE PROMPT IS THE ONE THAT WAS SENT AND NEVER A REBUILT ONE.
    `Eval::Realization::Bench#receipts_for` reads it off the `messages` rows the
    call left behind, which is what makes this the diagnosis half of a low hit
    rate: reading "asked for a cellar" here and seeing `none` come back is a
    finding, and a bare fraction is only a complaint.

    THE INSTRUCTION BLOCK IS NOT HERE, only its digest at the top of the page.
    The stored row keeps `instructions_digest` rather than the block itself
    (`Eval::Realization::Bench::Reading#to_h`), which is the bench's choice and
    not this page's to overturn -- the block is the same on every sample of every
    kind, and `Playthrough::PromptVersion` is how two samples are told apart by
    it. %>
<% prompt = (sample.row["prompts"] || {})[call] %>
<% answer = (sample.row["answers"] || {})[call] %>
<details class="exchange">
  <summary>the <%= call %> prompt, as sent<%= " (#{prompt.to_s.length} characters)" if prompt.present? %></summary>
  <div class="body"><pre><%= debug_value(prompt, absent: "not recorded -- the conversation was not kept") %></pre></div>
</details>
<details class="exchange">
  <summary>the raw <%= call %> answer</summary>
  <div class="body">
    <pre><%= answer.present? ? JSON.pretty_generate(answer) : debug_value(nil, absent: "nothing came back") %></pre>
  </div>
</details>
